---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../site.config';
import { PROFESSIONAL_REVIEWS } from '../lib/editorial';
---
<InfoPageLayout title="Editorial Policy – Sources, Review and Corrections | AyTool"
  description="AyTool's publishing policy: source verification, AI assistance, independent review status, corrections, dates and attribution."
  path="/editorial-policy/" h1="Editorial and Review Policy">
  <p>AyTool publishes independent payroll tools and PRC exam guides to help readers understand
    calculations and plan applications. The <a href="/about/maintainer/">AyTool maintainer</a> is
    responsible for its public content and corrections.</p>
  <h2>Primary sources and recorded checks</h2>
  <p>Rules and schedules link to government issuances, statutory text or official announcements.
    A recorded source-check date describes a particular data review; it does not mean every later
    announcement has already been incorporated. References without an individual check date are
    identified as such. Later official notices take precedence over this summary.</p>
  <h2>Three different kinds of review</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Maintainer source checks:</strong> source transcription, consistency of dates and figures, and corrections to the guide.</li>
    <li><strong>Automated software checks:</strong> calculation cases, edge cases, internal links and publishing checks. Passing tests does not certify legal or professional correctness.</li>
    <li><strong>Independent professional review:</strong> a completed review by a person with relevant, verifiable background. It is named only for the pages and scope actually reviewed, with that person's permission.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>{PROFESSIONAL_REVIEWS.length === 0 ? 'No independent professional review is currently registered.' : 'Completed independent reviews are identified on the pages and scope they cover.'} A maintainer byline, AI assistance
    or an official-source link is not presented as expert approval.</p>
  <h2>AI assistance and original work</h2>
  <p>AI tools assist with code and draft text. Sources, calculations and the reason for a conclusion
    must still be inspectable. Data tables retain their source links; calculated statistics explain
    their numerator, denominator and exclusions. Historical data and worked examples are available
    from the <a href="/data/">data library</a> and <a href="/calculation-examples/">calculation examples</a>.</p>
  <h2>Dates, predictions and results</h2>
  <p>Updated means an editorial or relevant data change. Source checked means an actual recorded
    source review. A nightly rebuild does not create a new source review. Historical exam dates,
    future schedules, target release dates and confirmed results are labeled separately; an
    unpublished exam date is not generated by adding a year to the old one.</p>
  <h2>Corrections and complaints</h2>
  <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a> with the page, disputed statement
    and source. Material factual corrections identify the date, the earlier statement, what changed
    and the supporting record in the <a href="/corrections/">public correction log</a>.
    Typographical changes do not imply a new professional review.</p>
  <h2>External references and affiliations</h2>
  <p>Government links identify the source of a fact; they do not imply endorsement. A published
    institutional citation or professional review will be described only when it can be verified.
    Paid or commercial relationships relevant to a recommendation must be disclosed with it.</p>
  <p>For review proposals and citation materials, see <a href="/for-publishers/">For educators and publishers</a>.</p>
</InfoPageLayout>
